                "Medium": {
                  "description": "The kinds of thing a household holds.\n\nNamed rather than passed through as the server's own word, because a surface\ndrawing \"Series\" against one server and \"tvshow\" against another would be\nrendering a detail of which server this household runs.\n\n`Medium` rather than `Kind`, `Holding` or `Sort`: this product already calls the two\nrequest services a [`crate::media::Kind`], a request's suspension a\n[`crate::service::asking::Holding`], and what one line of a manifest is a\n`uninstall::Sort` — and one word meaning two things in one vocabulary is how a\nreader comes to trust the wrong one. The contract flattens every type name into one\nnamespace, so a clash there is a clash for anything reading it by name.",
                  "oneOf": [
                    {
                      "const": "film",
                      "description": "One film.",
                      "type": "string"
                    },
                    {
                      "const": "series",
                      "description": "A television series, rather than one episode of one.",
                      "type": "string"
                    },
                    {
                      "const": "episode",
                      "description": "One episode of a series.",
                      "type": "string"
                    },
                    {
                      "const": "other",
                      "description": "Something the server holds that is neither, and is not hidden for that.",
                      "type": "string"
                    }
                  ]
                },
